# What belongs in this repository is the source of the game and the documents that explain it.
# Everything below is something a machine wrote, something a tool cached, or something that is
# nobody's business but the machine it was made on.

# ── Dependencies and build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── The Steam port ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The desktop wrapper that carries the game onto Steam: an Electron shell, a Steamworks bridge
# and the packaging config. The game itself stays here and stays MIT; the wrapper that sells it
# does not, so it lives beside the repository rather than in it. Nothing in `src/` knows it
# exists — the wrapper reaches the game through `dist/`, the same bundle the website serves.
shear-line/

# ── Test and measurement output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# Every PNG in here is written by the browser suite, and `difficulty-curve.txt`, `economy.txt` and
# `frame-histogram.txt` by the tests that measure them. Regenerate the gallery any time with
# `npm run shots`. Committed, they put a diff on the repo every time the suite runs.
#
# The picture the README points at lives at `.github/screenshot.png` instead, and is checked in on
# purpose: a README whose image is gitignored shows a broken box to everybody except its author,
# who is the one reader with the file on disk.
screenshots/

# ── The workshop, not the game ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The specification the game was built from, the instructions for building it, and the log of
# having built it. None of it is needed to build, run, play or verify.
#
# `DECISIONS.md` goes with them. Comments throughout `src/`, `tests/` and `e2e/` cite it by number
# — "see DECISIONS D-105" and the like, around five hundred times — and those citations stay. A
# decision number is a stable identifier for a piece of reasoning whether or not the log travels
# with the code, and a comment that says *which* decision it came from is more use than one that
# says nothing. They are not broken links; there is simply no link.
docs/
BUILD.md
START-HERE.md
PROGRESS.md
CHANGELOG.md
DECISIONS.md

# One-off image-generation scripts. `dev/audio-debug.html` is NOT ignored and must not be: it is a
# bench instrument, but `e2e/audio.spec.ts` navigates to it, so ignoring the folder wholesale would
# leave a cloned repo unable to run the gate the README documents.
dev/*.ps1

# Scratch from measurement and probe runs.
probe-out.txt
*.log

# ── Agent and editor working state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Session data, local settings, memory and scratchpads: how the work was done, not what was made.
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Local-only and OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
